cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MarketTickStreamer.jl in your work, cite it as below."
title: "MarketTickStreamer.jl: provider-agnostic tick-by-tick market data acquisition and paced replay in Julia"
abstract: >-
  A Julia package for acquiring tick-by-tick market data as a scientific
  substrate: live WebSocket streaming and paginated historical REST backfill
  behind one provider-agnostic interface, an append-only crash-only raw layer
  with per-session provenance, compaction to per-symbol per-day CSV or Arrow
  on the venue's own calendar, and paced replay of a recording into the same
  channel type the live source produces. Adapters ship for Alpaca (US
  equities) and Binance (crypto spot). Analysis pipelines couple to a capture
  through a documented channel contract; the package supplies the flux and
  the guarantees, not the estimators.
type: software
